  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "GEOSAT Land/Ice Geophysical Data Records",
  "description": "GEOSAT Geophysical Data Records (GDR) - (Raw altimeter data merged with Navy Astronauts Group (NAG) ephemerides, corrected for path-length effects due to troposphere and ionosphere) cover approximately 24 hours each (14 or 15 complete revolutions) beginning and ending as close as possible to 72° north (maximum latitude). GDR's are similar to SEASAT and GEOS-3, but include full 10 per second data as well as 1 second averages. GDR's collected over land ice, as well as GDR's over ocean but flagged as \"bad\" are archived on a separate tape from the ocean GDR's. These land/ice GDR's are useful when combined with GEOSAT waveform data records (WDR's). Altimeter often fails to re-acquire lock when it moves from land or ice to ocean. GDR's contain sea surface height, geoid height, significant wave height, height offset for over land or over ice, solid/fluid tide and wet/dry troposphere corrections, ionosphere correction, and flags indicating reasons for quality test failures.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To merge raw altimeter data with Navy Astronauts Group (NAG) ephemerides, corrected for path-length effects due to troposphere and ionosphere.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23519433",
